
# SSH Brute Force Investigation Report

## Executive Summary

A review of SSH authentication logs identified a significant number of failed login attempts originating from multiple internal source hosts.

Analysis revealed patterns consistent with SSH brute-force activity targeting several destination systems.

No confirmed system compromise was identified; however, the volume of failed authentication attempts indicates elevated risk and warrants further monitoring.

## Investigation Details

### Data Source

SSH Authentication Logs

### Platform

Splunk Enterprise 10.4

### Time Range

